<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="description" content="Meet Context Keepers, five Paderborn University computer science students thinking critically about AI and software engineering.">
<title>Team Context Keepers | Agentic SE Lab</title>
<script>
try {
  const saved = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = saved || (matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
} catch (_) {}
</script>
<style>
:root{--accent:#E4007C}
[data-theme="light"]{--bg:#FFF8E7;--text:#1D1D1F;--muted:#5A5A5F;--card:#FFFFFF;--line:#e8dfcc;--soft:#f5eedc}
[data-theme="dark"]{--bg:#14142B;--text:#F4F1DE;--muted:#B8B5A7;--card:#1F1F3D;--line:#383853;--soft:#292947}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
html{scroll-behavior:auto}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.6}
a{color:var(--accent)}
a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:0.2rem solid var(--accent);outline-offset:0.2rem}
header{padding:2rem max(1.5rem,calc((100% - 70rem)/2));border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.topline{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:2rem}
h1{font-size:2.5rem;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .5rem}
h2{font-size:1.75rem;line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 .75rem}
h3{font-size:1.25rem;margin:.65rem 0 .15rem}
.tagline{color:var(--muted);margin:0}
nav{display:flex;gap:1.25rem;margin-top:1rem}
nav a{font-weight:650;text-decoration-thickness:.1em;text-underline-offset:.2em}
#theme-toggle{flex:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;background:var(--card);color:var(--text);padding:.65rem .9rem;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
main{max-width:70rem;margin:auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem}
section{margin-bottom:3.5rem}
.intro{max-width:46rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 1.75rem}
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(16rem,1fr));gap:1.5rem}
.member-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--card);box-shadow:0 .3rem 1rem #0000000d}
.member-card img{width:8rem;height:8rem;object-fit:cover;border-radius:50%}
.member-card h3{margin-top:1rem}
.study{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin:.1rem 0 .7rem}
.member-card p{margin:.5rem 0 1rem}
.hot-take{margin-top:auto!important;margin-bottom:0!important;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border-radius:.65rem;padding:.7rem .85rem;font-size:.9rem;font-weight:650}
.future-box{background:var(--soft);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:1rem;padding:1.5rem;max-width:56rem}
.future-box p{margin:.6rem 0 0}
footer{text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;padding:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
@media (max-width:700px){
  header{padding:1.5rem 1rem}
  .topline{flex-direction:column;gap:1rem}
  main{padding:2rem 1rem}
  .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="topline">
    <div>
      <h1>Context Keepers</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Five CS students, many ideas, and a healthy suspicion of code that “just works.”</p>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#team">Meet the team</a>
        <a href="#future-of-se">Our view on AI</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <button id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">🌙 <span>Night mode</span></button>
  </div>
</header>
<main>
  <section id="team">
    <h2>Meet the team</h2>
    <p class="intro">We’re five first-semester M.Sc. Computer Science students at Paderborn University. Our interests range from interfaces and machine learning to security—and our quality-control methods include checking the docs, reviewing the code, and rating the Döner.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="member-card">
        <img src="{{image:chirag-web.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Chirag">
        <h3>Chirag</h3>
        <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester, Paderborn University</p>
        <p>Chirag is interested in machine learning and cricket, and keeps a close eye on Paderborn’s Döner scene. His list of every Döner he has eaten in Germany, with ratings, is longer than his list of thesis ideas. For small tasks like tests and short scripts, he finds AI a real time-saver. In big projects, though, it can lose context and start guessing, so he treats it like a fast intern and checks its work.</p>
        <p class="hot-take">🔥 Prompt engineering is just writing clear requirements, and we were always bad at that.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="member-card">
        <img src="{{image:gouthami-web.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Gouthami">
        <h3>Gouthami</h3>
        <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester, Paderborn University</p>
        <p>Gouthami enjoys data visualisation and dancing; baking is another interest, even if her cakes don’t always rise. She learned more German from supermarket labels than from her German class. AI helps her understand new libraries and error messages, but its confident tone is no substitute for checking the documentation. She also worries that students may stop learning the basics if they lean on AI too heavily.</p>
        <p class="hot-take">🔥 If you can’t explain the code AI wrote, you didn’t build it—you copied a guess.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="member-card">
        <img src="{{image:krish-web.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Krish">
        <h3>Krish</h3>
        <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester, Paderborn University</p>
        <p>Krish is into MERN-stack web development, chess and playing piano. He has around a 2000 rating in bullet chess, which means he can make bad moves very fast. He sees AI as a useful helper for simple, repeated code and basic app scaffolding, but it sometimes calls functions that do not exist. Checking generated code is part of the job, not an optional finishing touch.</p>
        <p class="hot-take">🔥 A junior with three AI agents and no code review can break production.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="member-card">
        <img src="{{image:kushi-web.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Kushi">
        <h3>Kushi</h3>
        <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester, Paderborn University</p>
        <p>Kushi is interested in UI/UX design, drawing and travelling around Germany with the Deutschlandticket. She has visited eight German cities and got lost at every Hauptbahnhof. AI is great for turning an idea into a quick prototype, but its designs can feel repetitive. In her view, it may handle the first 80 percent of a UI; the final details, human judgement and thoughtful design still matter.</p>
        <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI will make every app look the same, so good design will be the most valuable skill in tech.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="member-card">
        <img src="{{image:om-web.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Om">
        <h3>Om</h3>
        <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester, Paderborn University</p>
        <p>Om is interested in cybersecurity, football and mechanical keyboards—and owns more mechanical keyboards than shoes. He finds AI-generated code fast, but warns that it can produce unsafe code just as quickly, including passwords placed directly in code. AI can be useful when developers know enough to spot mistakes. Security awareness and careful review are essential parts of using it responsibly.</p>
        <p class="hot-take">🔥 The first big AI agent hack hasn’t happened yet—and it will start with a README file.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="future-of-se">
    <div class="future-box">
      <h2>The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
      <p>As a team, we see AI as a powerful assistant for repetitive work, quick prototypes and exploring unfamiliar tools—not an excuse to stop understanding the software. It can confidently guess, miss context or generate insecure code, so human review, testing and solid fundamentals matter.</p>
      <p>In the next 5–10 years, we expect more developers to guide AI agents and spend less time typing every line. The hard, valuable work will be deciding what to build, checking whether it is correct and safe, and making it clear and accessible for people. Better requirements, thoughtful design and careful verification will keep the humans in the loop.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<footer>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. <span id="year"></span> · Context Keepers</footer>
<script>
const toggle = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
function updateToggle(){
  const dark = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === "dark";
  toggle.innerHTML = dark ? "☀️ <span>Day mode</span>" : "🌙 <span>Night mode</span>";
  toggle.setAttribute("aria-label", dark ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
}
updateToggle();
toggle.addEventListener("click",()=>{
  const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
  try { localStorage.setItem("upb-theme",theme); } catch (_) {}
  updateToggle();
});
document.getElementById("year").textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

